```java
    public static int bestRow(int[][] grid) {
        int best = 0;
        int bestSum = -1000000;
        for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
            int sum = 0;
            for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
                sum += grid[r][c];
            }
            if (sum > bestSum) {
                bestSum = sum;
                best = r;
            }
        }
        return best;
    }
```
   - 1 pt: Iterates over every row with a loop bounded by grid.length
   - 1 pt: Iterates over every element of the current row with bounds based on grid[r].length (or an enhanced for)
   - 1 pt: Accesses elements with the row index first and the column index second
   - 1 pt: Accumulates the sum of the current row (and resets it for each row)
   - 1 pt: Keeps track of the largest row sum seen so far, initialized so negative sums work
   - 1 pt: Compares the current row sum with the best using a strict comparison so ties keep the smaller index
   - 1 pt: Records the row index (not the sum) of the best row when a new best is found
   - 1 pt: Returns the row index after all rows have been examined
   - 1 pt: The method compiles with correct 2D array syntax and return type int

